  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>This is the shape of the whole codebase. The controller is deliberately thin - it translates HTTP into a call and back. The service creates one context per request and hands it to a pipeline of eight small nodes. The nodes are stateless singletons, so they can be shared across all requests safely; all mutable data lives in the context. Below the pipeline sit three helpers: validation rules, the bank client, and the repository. Dependencies point downward - each layer only knows the one beneath it.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
